                      Beyond the Walls           By: subhaan
-----------------------------------------------------------

For generations, the people of Stonewall City believed monsters lived beyond their giant walls.
A curious girl named Mira found an old map showing places outside the city. Instead of fighting monsters, she discovered abandoned towns, forests, and evidence that humans once traveled freely.
When she returned, many refused to believe her. Yet she continued sharing what she learned.
Years later, explorers followed her path and rebuilt connections with distant settlements.
The greatest prison was never the wall itself—it was fear.
